  "sections": {
    "BASICS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "An abscess is a localized collection of pus in a cavity formed by the disintegration of tissues.",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "An abscess spreads along the pathway of least resistance from the tooth apex, resulting in osteomyelitis:",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "If this infection perforates through the",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "cortex of the bone in which the tooth is encased, it can result in a cellulitis that can burst through the skin to create a cutaneous draining tract.",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "The drainage can also occur through the",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "alveolar mucosa, above the mucogingival line (parulis).",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Can involve any teeth; the maxillary fourth premolars are most commonly affected, followed by the canines and mandibular first molars.",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Periodontal disease can extend down the root of the tooth to the apex, infecting the pulp and resulting in endodontic involvement (perio-endo lesion).",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Systemic spread of bacteria (bacteremia and pyemia) and the persistence of inflammation can affect other organ systems.",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "A tooth root abscess can have an acute or chronic phase:",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Phoenix abscess—acute exacerbation of a",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "chronic periapical abscess.",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Can arise without the presence of bacteria (sterile abscess).",
              "pdf_page": 1425,
              "printed_page": 1343,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
